### Day 3-4: CLIP+BART Fusion Model (~10-12h)

#### [NEW] [14_train_clip_bart_fusion.py](file:///d:/Users/Mihir/Downloads/Documents/Mihir%20Codes/Dp_Project/scripts/text_processing/14_train_clip_bart_fusion.py)

#### Architecture Decision: **Option A — Prefix Fusion (Recommended)**

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **I strongly recommend Option A (Prefix Fusion)** for your timeline and constraints. Here's the comparison:

| | Option A: Prefix Fusion | Option B: Cross-Attention |
|---|---|---|
| **Complexity** | Low — add projection layer + concatenate | High — modify BART decoder internals |
| **Training** | Standard seq2seq loss | Requires custom decoder with new cross-attn layers |
| **VRAM** | ~4-5GB with LoRA | ~6-8GB (new attention layers) |
| **Implementation time** | 1 day | 2-3 days |
| **Research backing** | VL-BART, VisualGPT, BLIP use this | FLAMINGO-style, more powerful but complex |
| **Risk** | Low — proven pattern | Higher — more debugging |

**How Prefix Fusion Works**:

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    BART Encoder                       │
│                                                       │
│  Input: [IMG_1] [IMG_2] [IMG_3] [TRANSCRIPT] text... │
│         ↑       ↑       ↑                             │
│    projected CLIP embeddings                          │
│    (512 → 1024 via Linear)                            │
│                                                       │
│  The encoder attends to BOTH visual and text tokens   │
└──────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┘
                       │
                       ▼
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    BART Decoder                       │
│                                                       │
│  Cross-attention over encoder output                  │
│  (automatically attends to visual tokens too!)        │
│                                                       │
│  Output: "The equation shows ψ = ... (see diagram)"  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Model Code (core architecture)**:
```python
class CLIPBARTFusion(nn.Module):
    def __init__(self, bart_model, clip_embed_dim=512, bart_embed_dim=1024):
        super().__init__()
        self.bart = bart_model  # BartForConditionalGeneration (with LoRA)

        # Projection: CLIP embedding space → BART embedding space
        self.visual_projection = nn.Sequential(
            nn.Linear(clip_embed_dim, bart_embed_dim),
            nn.LayerNorm(bart_embed_dim),
            nn.GELU(),
            nn.Dropout(0.1),
        )

        # Learnable [IMG] token type embedding
        self.img_type_embed = nn.Embedding(1, bart_embed_dim)

    def forward(self, input_ids, attention_mask, clip_embeddings,
                n_images, labels=None):
        # 1. Get BART text embeddings
        text_embeds = self.bart.model.encoder.embed_tokens(input_ids)

        # 2. Project CLIP embeddings
        visual_embeds = self.visual_projection(clip_embeddings)
        visual_embeds = visual_embeds + self.img_type_embed.weight

        # 3. Prepend visual tokens to text tokens
        combined = torch.cat([visual_embeds, text_embeds], dim=1)

        # 4. Extend attention mask for visual tokens
        vis_mask = torch.ones(visual_embeds.size()[:2], device=device)
        combined_mask = torch.cat([vis_mask, attention_mask], dim=1)

        # 5. Run through BART encoder+decoder
        encoder_output = self.bart.model.encoder(
            inputs_embeds=combined, attention_mask=combined_mask
        )
        outputs = self.bart(
            encoder_outputs=encoder_output,
            attention_mask=combined_mask,
            labels=labels
        )
        return outputs
```

